<title>BCM Examples</title>


</HEAD>
<body>

<h1>Edit Override&nbsp;</h1>

<div id="overDiv" style="position:absolute; visibility:hidden; z-index:1000;"></div>

<hr>

<a name="top">

<!-- Begin Page Layout -->

</a>
    <p>In the Edit Override page, you can override the <b>Rate</b>, <b>Yield</b>
    and <b>Average Cycle Time</b> attributes of the selected operation. &nbsp;<br>
</p>
<table class="shadow" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="100%" border="0">
  <tr>
    <td class="tableHeader">&nbsp;What you can do</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      <table class="tableBorder" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="0" width="100%" border="0">
        <tr class="tableRow0">
          <td>
            <p class="Header2">Overriding Operation Item Attributes</p>
            <ol>
              <li>In the Supply Chain Search page, select the operation class of
                type <b>Manufacturing</b>. <br>
                The Supply Path page is displayed.
              <li>In the Supply Path Detail area of the Supply Path page, click
                the required supply chain element. 
              <li>From the menu list, select the <b>Edit Item Override</b>
                option.<br>
                The Edit Override page is displayed.
              <li>In the Edit Override page, you can override the following
                values:
                <ol>
                  <li>Rate </li>
                  <li>Average Cycle Time </li>
                  <li>Yield Type </li>
                  <li>Yield</li>
                </ol>
            </ol>
            <blockquote>
              <p><b>Note: </b>Enter a value between 0 and 1 in the <b>Yield</b>
              field. The Yield type can be either <b>Static</b> or <b>TimePhased</b>.
              From the <b>Yield Type</b> list, if you select <b>Static</b>, the <b>Yield</b>
              field is displayed. If you select <b>Static</b> Yield type, you
              can associate a yield calendar to that operation item override. If
              you select <b>TimePhased</b> Yield type, the <b>Yield</b> field is
              not displayed.</p>
            </blockquote>
            <ol start="5">
              <li>Click the <b>Reset to Default</b> button, if you wish to
                revert the override for the selected operation item. The
                Override will not exist any longer for the operation item
                combination and default values for the operation are considered.
              </li>
              <li>Click the <b>Save and Return</b> button to return to the
                Supply Path page. <br>
                The details of the Operation-Item Override are highlighted in
                the <b>Operation Details</b> area of the Supply Path page.</li>
            </ol>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
  </tr>
</table>

<a name="top">

